  "id": "a503a628-39e6-5996-a347-38fa2ffaa03a",
  "slug": "chicken-pot-pie-soup-with-pie-crust-dumplings-recipe-11775517",
  "name": "Chicken Pot Pie Soup with Pie-Crust Dumplings",
  "recipe_type": "soup",
  "brief_description": "This chicken pot pie soup with pie crust dumplings is the is just what you need for soup season. Folded pie-dough pieces play the part of bouncy dumplings. If you like, swap the Italian seasoning for chili powder or curry powder.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "On a lightly floured surface, roll pie crust into a 12-inch circle. Cut with a sharp knife or pizza cutter into 7 strips, then cut crosswise into 7 strips, discarding any scraps. You should have about 40 squares. Cover squares with plastic wrap."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "To form dumplings, working with 1 square at a time, lightly brush edges with water. Lift opposite corners to meet, then press to seal and form a triangle. Repeat with remaining squares, keeping dumplings covered with plastic wrap."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Whisk together broth and condensed soup in a large Dutch oven. Stir in chicken, frozen vegetables, Italian seasoning, pepper, and garlic powder. Bring mixture to a boil over medium-high heat, stirring occasionally. Reduce heat to medium. Cook, covered, stirring occasionally, until vegetables and chicken are heated through, about 3 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Gently stir dumplings into soup. Cook, uncovered, stirring occasionally, until dumplings are tender and soup is slightly thickened, 8 to 10 minutes. Garnish servings with fresh thyme and additional pepper."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 25,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 20,
